---
name: project-ccwatch
description: "ccwatch — Claude Code usage on Apple Watch (usage % complication + reset timer); repo ~/ccwatch, CI→TestFlight like FitX; signing gotchas hard-won 2026-07-15"
metadata: 
  node_type: memory
  type: project
  originSessionId: 1aa54cfe-a152-4033-981d-93211e1b41ff
---

ccwatch = Claude Code usage on the user's wrist. Fork of akashbangad/ccwatch → github AssiamahS/ccwatch, local ~/ccwatch. Mac daemon `ccwatchd` (launchd dev.ccwatch.daemon, ~/.local/bin, Bonjour _ccwatch._tcp, OS-assigned port; reads OAuth token via /usr/bin/security with ACL whitelist, no GUI prompt) → iPhone app → watch app (dual rings + reset countdown) → WidgetKit complications (5h % + live Text(timerInterval:) reset countdown, added 2026-07-15). Same CI-only TestFlight pipeline as FitX ([[project-fitx]]): XcodeGen project.yml, auto-version pre-push hook, macos-26 signing job, team QGMAWHX827.

Hard-won signing facts (evening of 2026-07-15, ~6 failed CI runs):
- **App Groups entitlement breaks xcodebuild cloud signing** with ASC API keys when the group doesn't exist — error is a MISLEADING "Authentication failed: bearer token". App groups have no public ASC API endpoint (/v1/appGroups = 404) and can't be created by API-key sessions. Fix: create the group + assign to App IDs manually in the developer portal FIRST. Proven by A/B on branch no-appgroup-test (archive succeeded the moment entitlements were stripped).
- **ASC API keys** (both issuer 9c44682c-3cc3-4791-bd10-a2d8935788db, p8s in ~/.appstoreconnect/private_keys/): KB93R49B9J = FitX's CI key, can WRITE via public API (bundle IDs, capabilities); 8RF7P8XRQ9 = 403 on public-API writes but signs fine in xcodebuild. App records can't be created by ANY key (web UI only).
- exportArchive "Error Downloading App Information" = missing ASC app record.
- Bundle IDs com.assiamah.ccwatch{,.watchkitapp,.watchkitapp.complications} all registered + APP_GROUPS capability enabled via API 2026-07-15.
- XcodeGen owns info-spec plists: CFBundleVersion must be declared as $(CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION) in project.yml info properties + CI seds run number before generate, else every upload retries build 1 (same trap as FitX).

Cloud sync (build 13+): daemon mirrors snapshots to secret gist 783d61c4a1737f6cad0c6fb0572614dc (GistPublisher, gh-CLI token, 5-min heartbeat); watch app falls back to gist when Bonjour fails; complication provider fetches gist on each 15-min timeline refresh — works anywhere, no Mac network needed. TestFlight: internal group "Sly Internal", tester pelotonysl@outlook.com.

**Why:** these failure modes are generic to every future watch/widget app the user ships through CI (FitX avoided them only because it has no app groups).
**How to apply:** before first TestFlight run of any new app: create ASC app record in web UI, create/assign any app groups in the portal, pre-register bundle IDs via API with KB93R49B9J.
