---
name: reference-ios-app-playbook
description: "THE complete iOS app recipe — read BEFORE building any new app; start from everything learned, not from boilerplate"
metadata: 
  node_type: memory
  type: reference
  originSessionId: d81c3ff8-9358-481e-a13a-facc50417670
  modified: 2026-08-12T08:35:07.418Z
---

**Every new iOS app starts from THIS full stack — never from an old template.**

- **Target iOS 26** (current, 2026). `deploymentTarget: iOS "26.0"`, `xcodeVersion: "26.0"`. Adopt Liquid Glass (`.glassEffect()`, `GlassEffectContainer`) where it fits the design. CI: ALL jobs on `runs-on: macos-26` (Xcode 26.5) — Apple requires the iOS 26 SDK for ASC uploads; macos-15 images carry Xcode 16 and produce stale builds.
- **No local Xcode** on this Mac (CommandLineTools only) — compile validation happens in CI, always include an unsigned build job.
- **XcodeGen**: project.yml is source of truth ([[xcodegen rules]]); `sed` CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION=$GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER into project.yml BEFORE `xcodegen generate` (plists are stamped at generation).
- **Signing (paid account, Team QGMAWHX827, pelotonysl@outlook.com)**: cloud-managed signing with ASC key **KB93R49B9J** (`~/.appstoreconnect/private_keys/`) and **NO dev p12** (mixed = "Cloud signing permission error" — see [[feedback-asc-cloud-signing-recipe]]). Secrets: ASC_KEY_ID / ASC_KEY_P8 (base64 of p8) / **ASC_ISSUER_ID = `9c44682c-3cc3-4791-bd10-a2d8935788db`** (confirmed working 2026-07-30 with KB93R49B9J).
- **CI recipe**: copy `~/carplay/.github/workflows/ci.yml` (NOT vs-app's — it carries the cert-cap disease) — unsigned compile job + **archive UNSIGNED** (`CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=""`) then `exportArchive` with `-authenticationKeyPath/-KeyID/-KeyIssuerID` does the cloud distribution signing. Do NOT put `CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY="Apple Distribution"` on a cloud-signed archive with automatic signing — "conflicting provisioning settings", ARCHIVE FAILED (lastlegjet 2026-08-21). Archiving WITH cloud signing (no override) works but mints a throwaway "Created via API" DEVELOPMENT cert; cap = 10 → fleet-wide "Choose a certificate to revoke". Purge recipe: DELETE /v1/certificates for type DEVELOPMENT + name "Created via API" (keep the real personal cert).
- **ASC records**: use the **asc MCP** (~/asc-mcp/server.py, user-scope) — `new_app_setup` does bundle repoint + internal group + tester in one call for every fresh record; `apps` audits all records for missing tester groups. NEVER skip this: new records have zero groups and send no TestFlight email. (Raw-API fallback: PATCH /v1/apps pre-release, POST /v1/betaTesters with group inline.)
- **ATS for the Mac rig**: `NSAllowsLocalNetworking` + `NSExceptionDomains: tail40af16.ts.net` (subdomains, insecure HTTP). NEVER granular keys alongside NSAllowsArbitraryLoads ([[feedback-ats-granular-keys-kill-arbitrary-loads]]). Mac's Tailscale name: `saints-macbook-air.tail40af16.ts.net`, IP 100.97.199.99; iPhone is on the tailnet.
- **Watch targets**: arm64_32 — Int is 32-bit, Int(epoch-ms) traps on device only ([[feedback-arm64-32-watch-int-trap]]).
- **Traps**: `~/music` == `~/Music` (case-insensitive APFS) — never clone repos with library-colliding names into ~; repos may carry auto-version pre-push hooks that amend commits (fitx, partyrock, vs-app).
- **Existing app clients to crib from**: VS (~/vs-app → AssiamahS/music, talks to visualSerato :8795), amapiano-ios, ccwatch (watch), pmOS, scipioapp.
---
